Why isn't there more net traffic about rogues?  These are GREAT
characters-- the most fun character I've played to date (obligatory
credentials: I've won with a wizard, using the infinite gold cheat,
and with a barbarian and a rogue, fair and square).

What I like about rogues:

You sense the presense of spoliers--More--

great start up stats.  you always start out with max or near max
dexterity, the most important startup stat in the game, IMHO.
Adequate strength is always easily built up with training and
proper diet.  Not wasting startup stats on strength allows room
for other useful stats that allow fruitful spell casting, hit
point/power building, and prayer/sacrificing (exception to that
sacrificing: I once sacrificed a gray unicorn on a neutral altar
and got a message, like: This is an insult to Neutrality!--More--You
feel foolish!--More--Goodbye level 7.)

great intrinsics.  you get stealth and speed for free. Other
useful intrinsics also come quickly.  Eat all the human corpses
you like, the aggravate monster intrinsic will never affect you.

useful start-up weapons.  The short sword is okay for the monsters
you meet early on, and the daggers are good to throw at monsters
early on.  The potion of poison can be used to poison the first
large batch of darts you can accumulate, which will help you to
survive until you can find an altar.

easy alignment.  it's practically obligatory for a rogue to rob a
shop.  I would build up to exp level 10, get Stormbringer (also
easy with a rogue), come back, and just kill the shopkeepers--
always reliably easy, once you're familiar with the right
precautions.  Pick and choose the best booty and then go
downstairs and donate the useless money to somebody's temple.

I don't care to re-play character classes once I've won with them,
but certainly, I had the most fun with Proteus the Rogue.

